      "text": "To find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) for the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\)**:\n   - Start with the equation \\( y = 3x - 8 \\).\n   - Solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n     \\[\n     y = 3x - 8\n     \\]\n     Add 8 to both sides:\n     \\[\n     y + 8 = 3x\n     \\]\n     Divide both sides by 3:\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, the inverse function is:\n     \\[\n     f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Set \\( f(x) \\) equal to \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) and solve for \\( x \\)**:\n   - We need to solve the equation:\n     \\[\n     f(x) = f^{-1}(x)\n     \\]\n   - Substitute \\( f(x) \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) into the equation:\n     \\[\n     3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n     \\]\n   - To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides by 3:\n     \\[\n     3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n     \\]\n   - Simplify the left side:\n     \\[\n     9x - 24 = x + 8\n     \\]\n   - Subtract \\( x \\) from both sides:\n     \\[\n     8x - 24 = 8\n     \\]\n   - Add 24 to both sides:\n     \\[\n     8x = 32\n     \\]\n   - Divide both sides by 8:\n     \\[\n     x = 4\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verify the solution**:\n   - Substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the original function \\( f(x) \\):\n     \\[\n     f(4) = 3(4) - 8 = 12 - 8 = 4\n     \\]\n   - Substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):\n     \\[\n     f^{-1}(4) = \\frac{4 + 8}{3} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\n     \\]\n   - Since \\( f(4) = 4 \\) and \\( f^{-1}(4) = 4 \\), the solution is verified.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
